add('Medium','Reproduced; stored-data encoding','Currency symbols and some names contain mojibake',['/currencies','/event','/guide','/transfer'],'Read the currency symbols and affected names/dropdown choices.','The Euro symbol renders as corrupted text rather than €. Several older symbols and accented names are also corrupted; new sample symbols render correctly.','Repair the affected stored encoding and maintain consistent UTF-8 handling.','resources/views/currencies/index.blade.php');
findings[16].status = 'Fixed; backed-up data repair verified 2026-10-17';
findings[16].evidence += ' Resolution: the connection already uses UTF-8. Backed up exact original rows to storage/app/ui-audit/ui17-encoding-backup.json, then transactionally reversed valid Latin-1/Windows-1252 mojibake sequences in 150 targeted text fields across 149 rows: 7 currency fields, 138 archived event names and 5 transfer names. No guide name required repair. Every other field, including IDs, rates, amounts, timestamps and archived status, was verified unchanged. scripts/repair-ui17-encoding.php --verify confirmed all rows against the backup; a rescan found no further reversible errors in the targeted fields. LegacyEncodingRepairTest passed 1 test/34 assertions for valid text and single/double/mixed encoding. tests/Browser/legacy-encoding.cjs passed Euro and active accented transfer text/search plus Event/Guide rendering; archived names were verified in stored data, not via active list visibility. The repair does not guess irreversibly damaged characters or normalize unrelated database fields. Original observation above is retained as audit history.';
